# Line endings: LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default on a
# GitHub Windows runner) gets CRLF, and vitest then fails to parse the
# scripts/*.mjs modules the lint tests import: five suites died with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" before this rule existed.
# Reproduced by converting one of those files to CRLF on macOS and running
# its test. bash also refuses a CRLF script, so gate.sh and package.sh
# depend on this too.
#
# Nothing in the tree changes on macOS or Linux: every file is already LF,
# and `git add --renormalize .` produces no diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures and assets, so the rule above never touches them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.las binary
*.laz binary
*.e57 binary
*.pcd binary
*.ply binary
*.glb binary
*.tif binary
*.bin binary
# Exclude generated release artifacts from `git archive` source exports.
# The release/ tree is npm-run-package output (checksums, manifest, deploy/
# source zips); it must never ship inside the source zip.
/release/ export-ignore
# Anchored, and docs/release/ explicitly re-included. The unanchored form also
# matched docs/release/, so RELEASE_ASSETS.md — documentation whose whole job is
# to tell a reviewer how to verify the release — was stripped from the very
# archive it ships in.
docs/release/** -export-ignore

# Keep pre-release working notes out of `git archive` source exports.
#
# READINESS_REPORT_* lists the open blockers and the steps that must happen
# before a tag — working notes for cutting a release, not a record of what
# shipped, and nothing public links to it. The public surface is
# KNOWN_LIMITATIONS + VALIDATION_REPORT, which state what the release does and
# does not establish.
READINESS_REPORT_*.md export-ignore

# Superseded per-release evidence. The archive should carry the reports for the
# version it IS, not a pile of prior ones a reader has to date-sort. Kept in
# the repository and in history.
#
# NOT excluded: VALIDATION_REPORT_v0.5.9.md, which this release inherits its
# terrain/measurement claims from and which README and ARTIFACT_EVALUATION
# link to. It is load-bearing evidence, not clutter.
VALIDATION_REPORT_v0.6.0-alpha.1.md export-ignore
REPRODUCIBILITY_v0.6.0-alpha.1.md export-ignore
# The scholarly archive carries exactly one truth-document set — the shipped
# version's. Every prerelease notes/limitations/reproducibility/validation
# file stays in git history and on GitHub, but out of the deposit, so a
# researcher is never unsure which evidence applies to v0.6.0 (and the alpha.2
# validation report's link to a since-removed working note cannot dangle in
# the archive).
RELEASE_NOTES_v0.6.0-alpha.*.md export-ignore
KNOWN_LIMITATIONS_v0.6.0-alpha.*.md export-ignore
REPRODUCIBILITY_v0.6.0-alpha.*.md export-ignore
VALIDATION_REPORT_v0.6.0-alpha.*.md export-ignore
# The docs-site prerelease pages are the same history — one page per release,
# and the deposit carries only the shipped one.
docs-site/releases/v0.6.0-alpha.*.md export-ignore

# Superseded standalone release notes from earlier lines (v0.4.x, v0.5.x) are
# development history, not part of the v0.6.0 deposit. VALIDATION_REPORT_v0.5.9.md
# is deliberately kept: this release inherits its terrain/measurement validation.
RELEASE_NOTES_v0.4.*.md export-ignore
RELEASE_NOTES_v0.5.*.md export-ignore
# Their docs-site wrapper pages go with them. Each wrapper is nothing but an
# `@include` of the notes file, so shipping the page without the notes leaves a
# dangling include in the archive — the same shape as the alpha pages above.
# The sidebar is generated by reading the releases directory, so it follows.
docs-site/releases/v0.4.*.md export-ignore
docs-site/releases/v0.5.*.md export-ignore
# The release checklist is an internal process aid, not scholarly content.
docs/project/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md export-ignore

# The v0.7 implementation ledger is an internal chronological log of every
# defect and item of the release, one account per revisit. V070_CURRENT_STATUS.md
# is generated from it (scripts/gen-v070-status.mjs) and means nothing without
# it. Both stay in the repository and in history, and out of the source archive.
# The checks that read them (lint:known-limitations, lint:v070-status) skip with
# a printed notice when run from an archive, and still fail in a git checkout.
docs/releases/V070_IMPLEMENTATION_LEDGER.md export-ignore
docs/releases/V070_CURRENT_STATUS.md export-ignore

# Keep TypeScript/source as text so a stray byte never flips a diff to binary
*.ts text
*.tsx text
*.mjs text
